    "done_when": "docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-artifact-authoring-route.html answers the plan's open question jt60sa-artifact-authoring from the code, read-only. It reads /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/nova/imas/machine_artifact.py, nova/imas/mast_geometry.py publish_refined_artifact and its callers, and imas_ambix/gs/artifact_resolution.py author_pinned_description. It states whether any nova entry materializes a verified machine artifact from DD-shaped IDS input for an arbitrary machine (the §4 stores at /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/machine_description/OP1 and OP2 are DD 4.1.1 netCDF IDSs), naming the entry, its inputs, what it writes and how it is verified. Or it states what generic entry is missing and which repository owns adding it. It names the files a JT-60SA authoring route in ambix would touch, and whether the route can stay inside ambix. It runs one read-only probe: where an entry exists, materialize a JT-60SA artifact from the OP1 store into a directory under the run directory and report its manifest and digests; where none exists, show the call that fails and why. Nothing is written in nova, maps/ or any cache; the probe runs on the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set).",
